WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:03.820
A vessel develops under moving blood, while tiny

00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:07.225
endothelial projections meet the surrounding flow.

00:00:11.967 --> 00:00:15.852
Transparent zebrafish embryos let researchers observe

00:00:15.852 --> 00:00:19.518
cranial vessels developing within a living system.

00:00:24.758 --> 00:00:28.190
Primary cilia can act as biological structures

00:00:28.190 --> 00:00:28.787
relevant

00:00:28.787 --> 00:00:32.596
to mechanosensing. Their distribution changes during

00:00:32.596 --> 00:00:34.134
vascular development.

00:00:40.383 --> 00:00:44.379
The research combined vascular imaging with systematic

00:00:44.379 --> 00:00:47.856
assessment of endothelial cilia and hemodynamic

00:00:47.856 --> 00:00:48.670
conditions.

00:00:54.258 --> 00:00:57.741
My contribution was part of a wider collaborative

00:00:57.741 --> 00:01:01.141
research programme. No single clip proves every

00:01:01.141 --> 00:01:01.792
mechanism

00:01:01.792 --> 00:01:03.356
examined in the paper.

00:01:09.425 --> 00:01:13.199
Developmental biology begins with moving systems. A

00:01:13.199 --> 00:01:13.569
still

00:01:13.569 --> 00:01:17.048
image captures a moment, while flow changes the

00:01:17.048 --> 00:01:17.640
question

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:18.512
being asked.
